    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388-a1">

                <pb facs="0695" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg625"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 369.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. W. B. Gibbs to. Hon. G. G. Dibrell</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Union City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-02-04"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 4,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>:* * * Several parties here are anxious
                    to get information relative to the existing laws of Mexico in reference to
                    immigrants to that country, and on my own behalf, as well as for the benefit of
                    those here interested in knowing, I ask for— <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Reliable information as to the desire of Mexico to have
                            immigrants.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>How long does it require to become a naturalized citizen of
                            Mexico?</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Are any inducements in the way of homesteads or land grants offered by
                            the Government to actual settlers who become citizens; and, if so,
                            what?</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Are immigrants from the United States received without prejudice, or
                            are they regarded with suspicion by the Government or the people?</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>At what prices can large grants of land suitable for colonization be
                            obtained in the provinces of Sinaloa, Durango, or Chihuahua?</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>Of the high plains or elevated plateaus, what part is best watered and
                            most fertile, and what diseases are most prevalent?* * *</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. B. GIBBS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
